## [ENT-074] | 2026-11-17 04:14 UTC | Apollo | error | ref: game/fleet/mine.py | see: queue.log ENT-132
Class: a step that ends a run without ending what the run started (the family of ENT-066 and ENT-071: a run's end leaves a state that closes the next work).
Case: at 2026-11-17 03:50 UTC I ended two haulers' gather runs with the run host's stop file (queue.log ENT-132) to carry plate and boards to the Fleet Admiral's flagship (requests.log ENT-189). The runs ended, but the engine's mining loop of each ran on (GET /accounts/<pilot>/loop: running true, at 04:00 UTC): the stop leaves mine.py at a sleep, and its DELETE of the loop stands after the loop's wait, not in a finally. My catch script's goal answered 409 "A loop is running on this account" twelve times and then waited for a dock the loop never gave.
Effect: the delivery started at 04:03 UTC instead of about 03:52; one hauler was back at the field when its stage step ran and gave nothing on its first try. No credit lost; about 11 minutes of two ships.
